\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.17}{\ignorespaces Dynamic-network proxy visualizations for GSE287331.}}{26}{figure.caption.48}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.18}{\ignorespaces Overlay of $\Delta \beta $ (Adjacent--Normal) density curves across the three datasets, computed on the 326{,}330 CpG sites shared by all cohorts. All distributions are tightly centred around zero, indicating that the Adjacent--Normal shift is globally subtle yet consistent in shape across studies.}}{30}{figure.caption.56}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.19}{\ignorespaces Pairwise $\Delta \beta $ (Adjacent--Normal) concordance across the three methylation datasets. (a)~GSE69914 vs.~GSE287331 shows a mild positive monotonic trend, (b)~GSE69914 vs.~GSE225845 exhibits near-zero correlation, and (c)~GSE287331 vs.~GSE225845 similarly shows weak agreement. Together, these comparisons highlight cohort-specific variability in locus-level methylation drift, despite stable global A--N directionality. }}{31}{figure.caption.58}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.20}{\ignorespaces Two views of the t-SNE embedding computed on the 326k CpGs shared across GSE69914, GSE225845, and GSE287331. (a) Colouring by dataset reveals strong study- and platform-driven clustering, indicating that global methylation structure is dominated by inter-cohort effects. (b) Colouring by tissue state (Normal vs. Adjacent) shows a subtle within-dataset displacement of Adjacent samples, consistent with early localised methylation drift at the tissue margins. }}{32}{figure.caption.60}%
